  "dtb_rpb_rules": "Decision-token branching (DTB) and its random-position placebo (RPB): lexer, entropy, position and token rules.\n\nREQUEST 1 (T 1.0, top_p 1, max_tokens 48, logprobs 20) returns body token ids b[0..m-1] and the top-20 log probs at\neach position. Position j is ELIGIBLE iff its token text is not whitespace-only and its first non-whitespace\ncharacter starts in CODE state (a token that opens a comment or a string is eligible; tokens inside are not).\nDTB: j* = argmax_j H_j over eligible positions (ties -> earliest); RPB: j* uniform over eligible positions\n(rng default_rng([seed, arm, call, 4])). Candidates: ranks 2..8 of the top-20 at j*, minus special ids, backtick\ntokens, whitespace-only tokens and function-closing tokens. FORCED = uniform draw (rng [seed, arm, call, 3]).\nEmpty candidate set: DTB moves to the next-highest-entropy eligible position; RPB redraws (<= 10 times).\nFewer than 2 eligible positions, or no candidate anywhere -> NO_BRANCH (the unforced sample is kept).\nPositions are 0-based here; the plan's 1-based j* equals j + 1.\n",
  "special_min_id": 151643,
  "prompt": {
    "task_docstring": "Builds a short closed tour for the Travelling Salesman Problem by greedy construction. The tour starts at city 0. At every step select_next_node is called with the current city, the destination city (city 0, where the tour ends), the set of unvisited cities and the n x n numpy array of Euclidean distances, and it returns the next city to visit, one element of unvisited_nodes. When no city is left the tour returns to city 0. Instances have 50 to 100 cities uniform in the unit square; shorter total tour length is better.",
    "spec_doc": "Return the next city to visit: one element of unvisited_nodes.",
    "instruction_k1": "Write select_next_node_v1.",
    "instruction_k2": "Write select_next_node_v2.",
    "idea_k1": "Write select_next_node_v1 based on an idea different from the function above.",
    "idea_k2": "Write select_next_node_v2 based on an idea different from both functions above.",
    "prefill_k2": "```python\ndef select_next_node_v2(current_node, destination_node, unvisited_nodes, distance_matrix):\n    \"\"\"Improved version of select_next_node_v1.\"\"\"\n",
    "sha256_templates": "1a1e4c3c702b56e89444f716704ca1114c5da8ca4760333179ca7ab3fb8bb15d"
  },
  "C_table": {
    "A": "largest C* in {2000, 1500, 1000} with T1.0, T1.6, DTB, RPB and IDEA on both seeds (NOSEL 500 only if C* >= 1500)",
